        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "' Varradene'  is a substantial and immensely appealing, double fronted, four bedroomed semi-detached family home enjoying a mature, well established residential location. With a wealth of bright, carefully  proportioned and versatile family sized accommodation, a great rear garden, and a practical side entrance, valuable off street parking in the cobble lock driveway accommodates a number of cars. Indeed should one so wish, the study / home office on the ground floor could be used as a 5th bedroom. Its' higher than average ceiling heights ( c 2.7m on the ground floor and c 2.55m on the first floor of the original house) add to it's wonderful sense of space and light. \r\nWith a hugely generous rear garden and a large attic, ample opportunity and scope exists to extend this lovely home still further if desired ( StoPP). \r\n\r\nIn the proud ownership of the same family for a long number of years, the lovingly maintained original house has been extended to the rear and now houses the kitchen.  The original garage now comprises a study/ home office / playroom or as above a  possible 5th bedroom and a guest wc, over which has been built a bedroom. \r\nSet out over two floors, the welcoming entrance porch and  hallway with guest cloakroom leads to a particularly spacious dual aspect, reception room extending from front to back of the original house. Previously two separate rooms, a fireplace in the front section of the room makes for a cosy sitting area and with a door to the garden,  the rear section of the room offers much flexibility of use.  This room, could of course be restored to provide separate / interconnecting reception rooms. The breakfast room which enjoys access from both the hall and the main reception room leads to the kitchen which in turn leads to the lovely rear garden. The study/ home office benefits from a private door via the side passage and so lends itself to easy access. \r\nOn the first floor, the two original front bedrooms now comprise the master bedroom and ensuite which was recently refitted.  Two further large double bedrooms and a generous single bedroom along with a bathroom and separate wc  make up the first floor. A large attic  ( floored and with Stira access)  provides an opportunity for conversion. \r\nA practical gated side entrance leads to the substantial well enclosed rear garden which is sheltered by magnificent mature trees providing an amazingly quiet and private oasis of calm. Benefitting from an exceptionally private aspect, this super family sized rear garden with its expansive lawn could easily provide a new owner with ample opportunity to further extend. \r\n\r\n'Varradene' enjoys an enviable location with a vast selection of educational, recreational and shopping amenities nearby.  Neighbourhood shops are just a  few minutes stroll on Bird Avenue/ Dundrum Road. Dundrum Town Centre, Stillorgan SC  and the Beacon SC are easily accessible.  Renowned for some of Dublin's best and most highly regarded schools and colleges -  those within easy reach include UCD, Our Lady’s Grove, Goatstown Educate Together, Eurocampus ( St. Killians German and Lycee Francais International French schools) , Alexandra College, Muckross Park, Mount Anville, Sandford National, Sandford Park  and  Gonzaga. Near-by sports and leisure  facilities include Milltown, Elm Park, The Grange, Edmondstown and Rathfarnham Golf Clubs,  the wonderful facilities of UCD,  David Lloyd Riverview, Darty Health Club, Brookfield Tennis Club, the Cinema and Theatre at Dundrum.\r\nRanelagh, Donnybrook, Rathmines and Rathgar are all within an easy commute as indeed are Stillorgan and Sandyford Business / Office Parks. \r\nA wonderful selection of parks, many with children's playgrounds abound in the area  -  Airfield, Palmerston Park, Bushy Park, the lush leafy 32 acres of Deer Park and the walkways of the Dodder Linear Park make this a truly enviable location.  The outstanding Marlay Park encompassing the  historic 18th Century Marlay House, Demesne and Regency Walled Garden which also offers super kids  playgrounds, cycling / walking trails, and various sports facilities including tennis courts, football pitches and cricket grounds is within easy reach. The beautiful Marlay House often host various cultural and heritage events throughout the year. \r\nWell worth a visit -  Marlay Park week-end Farmers Market is located behind Marlay House and its charming craft courtyard.\r\n\r\nPublic transport options offering excellent connectivity include the Green Line Luas ( stations at Windy Arbour and Milltown). A number of bus routes including  the 44, S4, 44D, 142 and 11, traverse the locale. Access to the N11 and M50 road networks are provided locally."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation\r\nEntrance  porch \tDouble glazed porch with sliding door and tiled floor. Original front door to \r\n\r\nReception hall      Guest wc. Original picture rail. Stairs to first floor. \r\n\r\nLounge/ Dining room \tMost attractive reception space offering dual aspect with large picture window overlooking front garden and half glazed door / windows to rear.  Marble fireplace with matching hearth.  Picture rail.  Georgian style glazed door to \r\n\r\nBreakfast room\tFitted storage and desk. Arch to\r\n\r\nKitchen\t\tFitted floor and wall units.  Stainless steel sink and drainer. Plumbed for washing machine and dishwasher. Mostly tiled walls. Large window overlooking the garden and semi glazed door to rear garden.\r\n\r\nStudy/ Home office / Playroom/ Bedroom 5  Versatile space to front. Door and glass block wall to side passage. Fitted storage with sliding doors. Access to understairs store. \r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\nLanding\t\t        Shelved hot press. Picture rail.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\t\tTo front. Originally 2 bedrooms now combined to wonderful master suite.  Extensive fitted wardrobes, vanity unit and fitted mirror / shelves /  storage.   \r\nEnsuite\t\t\tRecently fitted with white 3 piece suite incorporating shower cubicle with bi-fold door and Triton Novel SR shower,  wc with concealed    cistern and vanity whb with Grohe monobloc.  Tiled floor and part tiled walls. Window.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\t\tTo rear. Large double/ twin.  Window over-looking rear  garden. Fitted whb. Picture rail. Access to attic\r\n\r\nBedroom 3\t\tGenerous single to rear. Fitted wardrobes and vanity unit with whb. Fitted storage / shelving..\r\n\r\nBedroom 4 \t\tTo front.  Now laid out to accommodate a single bed, it could be transformed to an excellent double. Fitted wardrobes with sliding  doors. Fitted recessed shelves. Whb  . \r\n\r\nBathroom \t\tBath and whb with Triton electric shower over. Window.\r\nSeparate wc. \tWindow.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\nTo the front the extensive paving provides valuable off-street parking for a number of cars and  is bordered by mature shrubs including a  welcoming picturesque  summer flowering Wisteria. The  gated side entrance ensures easy and practical access for bikes and bins, maintenance and gardening. The impressive lawned rear garden exudes a marvellous sense of privacy with a selection of trees and bushes. Two patio areas  -  one raised directly outside the kitchen offers an easy al fresco dining option and one exceedingly sheltered area to the rear of the main reception room almost provides an extensions to the living accommodation.  There is also a wooden storage shed."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
